Fix: stale stock cache lets checkout authorize payment for stock that no longer exists

Release 1.4.0 cached stock levels for 10 minutes. After a warehouse sync lowered
stock in the database, checkout still read the cached (higher) value, authorized
the card, then failed on the CHECK (stock >= 0) constraint and rolled back,
leaving an orphaned payment authorization.

- availableStock() reads the authoritative value from the database
- reserve() uses a conditional decrement and throws OutOfStock instead of
  relying on the constraint
- checkout reserves stock before authorizing payment, in one transaction

Apply from demo-shop/:  patch -p1 < fixes/stale-stock-cache.patch

diff -ruN a/src/Catalog/ProductRepository.php b/src/Catalog/ProductRepository.php
--- a/src/Catalog/ProductRepository.php	2026-11-18 02:30:58.627400600 +0500
+++ b/src/Catalog/ProductRepository.php	2026-11-18 02:31:13.047985900 +0500
@@ -45,6 +45,16 @@
         return (int) $this->db->executeStatement('UPDATE product SET stock = stock - ? WHERE sku = ?', [$quantity, $sku]);
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Conditional decrement: succeeds only if enough stock exists at write time.
+     *
+     * @return int affected rows (0 = not enough stock)
+     */
+    public function reserveStock(string $sku, int $quantity): int
+    {
+        return (int) $this->db->executeStatement('UPDATE product SET stock = stock - ? WHERE sku = ? AND stock >= ?', [$quantity, $sku, $quantity]);
+    }
+
     /** Warehouse sync: sets the authoritative stock level directly in the database. */
     public function setStock(string $sku, int $stock): void
     {
